/ Settled-state streams, shared by the initial pay response and the poller so
/ the two paths can't drift. Swaps the action region for the result and announces
/ the outcome. On success it also refreshes the territory modal in place: a
/ trigger-less frame render, so a payment made from a closed modal updates the
/ content silently (the toast is all the player sees) rather than popping the
/ modal open. A failure has no refreshed_territory, so its in-place error trace
/ and retry button survive.
/ locals: command, target, current_server, refreshed_territory
= turbo_stream.replace target do
  = render "servers/territories/pay_result", command:

= pay_outcome_toast(command)

- if refreshed_territory.present?
  = turbo_stream.replace "territory_detail_frame" do
    = turbo_frame "territory_detail" do
      = render "servers/territories/detail", current_server:, current_territory: refreshed_territory
